          <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}\leftarrow\tilde{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{[a,b]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐬</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝜶</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}\leftarrow\tilde{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{[a,b]}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">

</span><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Stage 1: late-layer head-mean aggregation
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\star}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{s};K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒫</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐬</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\star}\leftarrow\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{s};K)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">; 
</span><math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}\leftarrow\textsc{Map}(\mathcal{P}^{\star},\mathcal{W}^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathsize="0.900em">Map</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒫</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}\leftarrow\textsc{Map}(\mathcal{P}^{\star},\mathcal{W}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">

</span><span id="alg1.l5.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> select top-<math id="alg1.l5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> patches; lift to char spans
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(1)}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}(T,\,\hat{\mathcal{E}},\,s_{\mathrm{font}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">font</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(1)}\leftarrow\mathcal{R}(T,\,\hat{\mathcal{E}},\,s_{\mathrm{font}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">

</span><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Stage 2: re-render with <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> enlarged
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
          <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{I}^{(1)},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">q</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}\leftarrow\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{I}^{(1)},q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">

</span><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> answer from the magnified page
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">return</span><span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 1 – Attention-Based Evidence Localization.</h4>

<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;"><img src="2606.12898v1/AGAR_final.png" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/210;" width="229" height="210" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>AGAR overview. Attention localizes evidence patches, which
are magnified on a re-rendered page for a second forward pass.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first render the textual context <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> at the baseline font size with
the renderer <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, obtaining the raw image
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> together with a word–bounding-box map
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}^{(0)}=\{(w,\beta_{w},[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e}))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}^{(0)}=\{(w,\beta_{w},[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e}))\}</annotation></semantics></math>
(Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line <a href="#alg1.l2" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) that records, for
every rendered word <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>, its image-space box <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and the
character span <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e})</annotation></semantics></math> it occupies in <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. A single
forward pass of the VLM on <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{I}^{(0)},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{I}^{(0)},q)</annotation></semantics></math> with
<span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">output_attentions=True</span> yields the layer-wise attentions
(Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line <a href="#alg1.l3" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), which we collapse
into a per-patch score
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}=\tilde{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{[a,b]}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜶</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}=\tilde{\boldsymbol{\alpha}}_{[a,b]}\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]=[0.5,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]=[0.5,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math> by default (Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
line <a href="#alg1.l4" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>; Obs. <a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 RQ1: In the VTC setting, where does evidence-localizing attention emerge inside a VLM? ‣ 3 Preliminary Studies ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). The top-<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> patches
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}^{\star}=\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{s};K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>TopK</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}^{\star}=\mathrm{TopK}(\mathbf{s};K)</annotation></semantics></math> live in the model’s
visual grid; since the unit we can actually magnify is a rendered word,
we <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">map</em> the selection from patches to character spans:
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}=\textsc{Map}(\mathcal{P}^{\star},\mathcal{W}^{(0)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">Map</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}=\textsc{Map}(\mathcal{P}^{\star},\mathcal{W}^{(0)})</annotation></semantics></math>
(Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line <a href="#alg1.l5" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>).
Concretely, <span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_smallcaps">Map</span> marks a word <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in\mathcal{W}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒲</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in\mathcal{W}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> as
selected whenever its box <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> overlaps any selected patch
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in\mathcal{P}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in\mathcal{P}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> (after rescaling <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> to the visual
encoder’s input resolution), collects the corresponding character spans
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>e</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[c_{w}^{\,s},c_{w}^{\,e})</annotation></semantics></math>, and merges overlapping/adjacent spans.
The output <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}\subseteq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⊆</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}\subseteq T</annotation></semantics></math> is our <em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">predicted</em>
evidence—the attention-only counterpart of the oracle <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> used
in Obs. <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 RQ3: How can we help the model better utilize the evidence it already localizes? ‣ 3 Preliminary Studies ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stage 2 – Magnified Re-rendering and Re-inference.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We re-invoke the renderer with <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of character
spans to draw at a magnified font size <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{font}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>font</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{font}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(1)}=\mathcal{R}(T,\,\hat{\mathcal{E}},\,s_{\mathrm{font}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>font</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(1)}=\mathcal{R}(T,\,\hat{\mathcal{E}},\,s_{\mathrm{font}})</annotation></semantics></math>
(Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, line <a href="#alg1.l6" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>), while keeping all
other typography and layout parameters identical to <math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>. We then produce the
final answer with one more forward pass,
<math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}=\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{I}^{(1)},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}=\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{I}^{(1)},q)</annotation></semantics></math> (Alg. <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,
line <a href="#alg1.l7" title="In Algorithm 1 ‣ 4 AGAR: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), and discard the first-pass output. This makes AGAR a model-agnostic plug-in for any VLM
that exposes layer-wise attentions. No prompt or weight changes are
needed.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate AGAR around four questions:
(i) does AGAR consistently improve VTC accuracy on off-the-shelf VLMs
across short-form, long-context, and multi-page memory QA
(§<a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>)? (ii) does its gain persist when the underlying VLM
is post-trained (§<a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Composing AGAR with Post-Training ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>)? (iii) is the gain robust
to low-quality input images and irrelevant text contexts
(§<a href="#S5.SS4" title="5.4 Robustness to Imperfect Inputs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>)? and (iv) how sensitive is AGAR to its two
core hyper-parameters, the patch budget <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and the magnification factor
<math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{font}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>font</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{font}}</annotation></semantics></math> (§<a href="#S5.SS5" title="5.5 Hyperparameter Analysis ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.5</span></a>)?</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Datasets.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We benchmark AGAR on three families of VTC tasks of increasing visual and
textual complexity. (i) <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Short-form QA</span>: NQ <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>,
HotpotQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> (distractor mode),
TriviaQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> (TQA), and
NewsQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, each rendered onto a single page.
(ii) <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LongBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite> multi-page QA</span>: HotpotQA-LB
(HQA), 2WikiMultihop <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> (2WMQA),
MuSiQue <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite> (MSQ), and
Qasper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> (QP), where the context spans multiple
rendered pages. (iii) <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LoCoMo <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>
multi-page memory QA</span>, which further stresses long, session-style
contexts. We use the official
validation/test splits and report EM and F1; per-dataset sample counts and
average context lengths are summarized in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Dataset Statistics ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>
(Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Dataset Statistics ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Models and Baselines.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our primary backbone is <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct</span>; cross-architecture
results on <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InternVL3.5-8B</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GLM-4.1V-9B-Thinking</span>, and
<span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Glyph</span> (post-trained on GLM-4.1V-9B-Thinking) are in
Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. We compare AGAR against three baseline groups:
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Plain VQA</em> (answers directly from <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>); two
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">naive baselines</em> that isolate AGAR’s two design choices —
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">random</em>, which magnifies <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> randomly chosen patches (tests
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">which</em> patches matter), and <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniform</em>, which scales the whole
page font to match AGAR’s visual-token count (tests whether token count
alone suffices); and prior emphasis methods adapted from VQA:
<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">VEA</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CGR</em>/<em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">VAR</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>,
and <em id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AGLA</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> (App. <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Baseline Implementation ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Pages render at <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>9</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9</annotation></semantics></math> px; AGAR uses late-layer range <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[a,b]=[0.5,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[a,b]=[0.5,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math> and
font scale <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{font}}=1.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>font</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{font}}=1.5</annotation></semantics></math>. The patch budget is <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=8</annotation></semantics></math> for
single-page short-form QA and <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!\approx\!2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!\approx\!2\%</annotation></semantics></math> of total patches for the
multi-page benchmarks (LongBench, LoCoMo). See examples in App. <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Case Study ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To answer question (i), we evaluate off-the-shelf Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct
on the abovementioned datasets. Short-form single-page QA results are
reported in Tab. <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Multi-page LongBench QA
and LoCoMo memory QA results are reported jointly in
Tab. <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. The two naive baselines (Random, Uniform) yield no or only marginal
gains over Plain VQA. This indicates that AGAR’s gain comes from
effectively selecting the important evidence to emphasize, rather than
simply increasing the number of visual tokens. The prior VQA-emphasis methods (VEA, CGR, VAR, AGLA) provide only
limited enhancement and underperform our method, and even hurt the
performance on some datasets. These methods are originally designed
for standard VQA, where <em id="S5.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">de-emphasising</em> irrelevant visual
background helps the answer. They thus import the wrong inductive bias
for VTC, in which the surrounding text must remain readable for full
context understanding.
AGAR, in contrast, delivers clear and consistent gains over Plain VQA
on every cell of both tables (e.g. <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+18.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>18.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+18.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> F1 on short-form
HotpotQA, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+28.5\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>28.5</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+28.5\%</annotation></semantics></math> on LB-MSQ multi-page, <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+38.8\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>38.8</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+38.8\%</annotation></semantics></math> on LoCoMo
OpenDomain) and strictly outperforms every baseline, while increasing
visual-token cost only marginally (maintaining
<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math> compression). The same observation holds for the
other three VLMs; see Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>,
Tables <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span><span id="S5.T2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Short-form single-page QA</span> on Qwen3-VL-8B. Each cell shows
the metric followed by its <em id="S5.T2.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">relative</em> change (%) vs. Plain VQA.
Avg. text tokens <math id="S5.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 805" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mn>805</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 805</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S5.T2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∼</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S5.T2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math> compression).</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T2.12" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:84.1pt;vertical-align:-40.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-102.4pt,25.0pt) scale(0.627451485354423,0.627451485354423) ;">
<table id="S5.T2.12.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T2.12.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
