<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Cross-Architecture Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that the AGAR gain is not specific to one architecture or
post-training recipe, we additionally evaluate three other VLMs:
<span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">InternVL3.5-8B</span>, <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GLM-4.1V-9B-Thinking</span>, and
<span id="A3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Glyph</span> (a public model post-trained from GLM-4.1V-9B-Thinking
specifically for visual text comprehension). Tables <a href="#A3.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>–<a href="#A3.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix C Cross-Architecture Results ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>
mirror Tables <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.2 Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>–<a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 5.2 Main Results: AGAR on Off-the-Shelf VLMs ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Magnifying What Matters: Attention-Guided Adaptive Rendering for Visual Text Comprehension" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
of the main text. The magnitude and direction of the gain track
the same patterns observed for Qwen3-VL-8B in the main text.</p>
</div>
